Design and implement a **frontend-only Earth–Moon orbital simulation** with production-quality code and deterministic, demonstrable behavior.

## Technical Specifications
1. **Tech Stack**
   - React 18+
   - TypeScript 5+
   - Vite (build tool)
   - HTML5 Canvas (for performant animation)
   - Tailwind CSS 3+ (UI controls and layout)
   - No backend dependencies

2. **Core Requirements**
   - Simulate the Moon orbiting the Earth using a simplified Newtonian gravitational model.
   - Render Earth and Moon in real time on a `<canvas>` with smooth animation via `requestAnimationFrame`.
   - Allow user control over simulation parameters (play/pause, time scale).
   - Ensure the code runs out-of-the-box with `npm install && npm run dev`.

---

## Application Structure
```
src/
 ├─ components/
 │   ├─ OrbitCanvas.tsx
 │   ├─ ControlPanel.tsx
 ├─ hooks/
 │   ├─ useAnimationFrame.ts
 ├─ models/
 │   ├─ physics.ts
 │   ├─ types.ts
 ├─ App.tsx
 ├─ main.tsx
 └─ index.css
```

---

## Data Models & Interfaces
```ts
// models/types.ts
export interface Vector2 {
  x: number;
  y: number;
}

export interface CelestialBody {
  id: 'earth' | 'moon';
  mass: number; // kg (scaled)
  radius: number; // px
  position: Vector2;
  velocity: Vector2;
  color: string; // hex
}

export interface SimulationState {
  isRunning: boolean;
  timeScale: number; // e.g. 1 = real-time, 10 = fast-forward
}
```

---

## Physics Model
```ts
// models/physics.ts
import { Vector2, CelestialBody } from './types';

export const G = 6.674e-11; // gravitational constant (scaled in simulation)

export function computeGravity(
  a: CelestialBody,
  b: CelestialBody
): Vector2 {
  const dx = b.position.x - a.position.x;
  const dy = b.position.y - a.position.y;
  const distSq = dx * dx + dy * dy;
  const dist = Math.sqrt(distSq);

  const force = (G * a.mass * b.mass) / distSq;
  return {
    x: (force * dx) / dist,
    y: (force * dy) / dist,
  };
}
```

---

## Canvas Rendering Component
```tsx
// components/OrbitCanvas.tsx
import { CelestialBody } from '../models/types';

interface OrbitCanvasProps {
  earth: CelestialBody;
  moon: CelestialBody;
  width: number;
  height: number;
}

export function OrbitCanvas({
  earth,
  moon,
  width,
  height,
}: OrbitCanvasProps) {
  return (
    <canvas
      id="orbit-canvas"
      width={width}
      height={height}
      className="bg-black rounded-lg border border-slate-700"
    />
  );
}
```

